From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 24 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: Do not build the WebAssembly stdlib on Linux

mixin_linux_installation asks for WasmKit and a WebAssembly standard
library, so every Linux toolchain build compiles a wasi-sysroot, a second
LLVM targeting wasm32, and the stdlib on top of it. This produces nothing
we use: the toolchains built here target Linux.

It also does not currently configure. The wasm stdlib is the one place
that reaches the string processing sources through a path with a
"swift/.." segment in it, and its configure ends with

  CMake Error at stdlib/cmake/modules/AddSwiftStdlib.cmake:1212:
    No SOURCES given to target: swift_RegexParser-wasi-wasm32

for each of _RegexParser, _StringProcessing and RegexBuilder, while the
Linux stdlib built from the same sources moments earlier.

Drop the three options rather than carry a build that costs hours and
fails at the end of them.
---
--- a/utils/build-presets.ini
+++ b/utils/build-presets.ini
@@ -861,7 +861,6 @@
 xctest
 swiftdocc
 swiftformat
-wasmkit
 
 build-ninja
 install-llvm
@@ -879,12 +878,10 @@
 install-sourcekit-lsp
 install-swiftformat
 install-swiftdocc
-install-wasmkit
 build-swift-static-stdlib
 build-swift-static-sdk-overlay
 build-swift-stdlib-unittest-extra
 build-embedded-stdlib-cross-compiling
-build-wasm-stdlib
 
 # Executes the lit tests for the installable package that is created
 # Assumes the swift-integration-tests repo is checked out
